# TEMPLATE for .syncignore (which is gitignored). Copy this to .syncignore and
# list your own private files, then sync.sh will exclude them from the public
# build.
#
#   cp .syncignore.example .syncignore   # then edit .syncignore
#
# The real .syncignore is gitignored on purpose: the filenames you exclude are
# themselves private-project references (a guide named after a private codename
# reveals the codename). This template carries only generic placeholders.
#
# Format: one path per line, relative to the destination subtree. Shell-style
# glob patterns are supported (a trailing /** removes the whole directory).
# Add anything that references private projects, proprietary data, or personal
# contact info that simple scrub rules (scrub.sh) can't sanitize.

# --- commands/ ---
# Personal/hobby slash commands that won't generalize.
commands/your-private-command.md

# --- hooks/ ---
# Hooks that hardcode private infrastructure (DB project refs, schema names).
hooks/your-private-hook.sh

# --- reference/ (from your dev-reference library) ---
# Whole directories of personal scratch.
reference/tmp/**
reference/voice/**

# Project-internal conventions/guides/workflows named after private codenames
# or tied to one proprietary system.
reference/conventions/your-internal-convention.md
reference/guides/your-private-codename-guide.md
reference/workflows/your-internal-runbook.md
reference/templates/your-examples-with-real-names.md
